msgid "Keyboard shortcuts"
msgstr ""

msgid "*Every key and gesture of EMStudio, grouped by where it acts.*"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The same list is in the application under ``Help ▸ Shortcuts``, where you"
" can search it. The tables below are drawn from the same source, so they "
"say what the application does."
msgstr ""

msgid "Where a key acts"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A key acts on the part of the window that has the focus, and the tables "
"are grouped the same way."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Everywhere**: the keys of the whole application, such as saving, the "
"settings, the chip's menu at **Where you work** and adding a node."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**On the graph**: the keys of a Graph window (the matrix, the free graph,"
" the DTC) and of the Outliner. They act on the canvas and on the "
"Outliner, and leave a field you are typing in, or a focused button, "
"alone."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**In the Space**: the keys of the 3D scene when it has the focus. They "
"follow the conventions of Blender, so that whoever models in Blender "
"finds the same hands here: :kbd:`G`, :kbd:`R` and :kbd:`S` move, rotate "
"and scale, the numeric keypad chooses the views, :kbd:`⇧A` adds a shape "
"at the 3D cursor."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Tracing in the document**: the keys of the Viewer while you trace a "
"region on an image."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Windows and spaces**: the gestures that arrange the windows and the "
"workspaces."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**In a field** and **in menus and buttons**: the keys of typing and of "
"moving through a menu."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The same key can mean different things in different places: :kbd:`⇧A` "
"adds a node to the graph when the pointer is on the matrix, and a shape "
"to the scene when the 3D has the focus."
msgstr ""

msgid "Keys and gestures"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The keys are given as the Mac shows them and as Windows and Linux show "
"them: ⌘ (Command) becomes :kbd:`Ctrl`, ⌥ (Option) becomes :kbd:`Alt`, ⇧ "
"is :kbd:`Shift`. A gesture (a click, a drag, the wheel) is described in "
"words and is the same on every platform; where its description names ⌘ or"
" ⌥, read :kbd:`Ctrl` or :kbd:`Alt` on Windows and Linux."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"On the web the browser keeps some keys for itself, for example the one "
"that closes the tab: the last table, *In the menus*, says which keys the "
"menus show and which of them the web leaves to the browser."
msgstr ""

